Package: spifa
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Spatial Item Factor Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Encoding: UTF-8
Authors@R: c(
    person(c("Erick", "A."), "Chacón-Montalván", , "erick.chaconmontalvan@wur.nl",
        role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8068-1034")),
    person("Emanuele", "Giorgi", role = "ctb"),
    person("Benjamin M.", "Taylor", role = "ctb"))
Description: Fits spatial item factor analysis models for binary responses,
    following Chacón-Montalván, E. A. et al. (2025) <doi:10.1214/25-AOAS2072>,
    using full Bayesian inference via adaptive Metropolis-Hastings within
    Gibbs sampling and auxiliary variables with a probit link function. The
    latent factors are modelled as the sum of a predictor effect, a
    multivariate Gaussian process capturing spatial dependence, and a
    multivariate non-spatial term, allowing users to fit and predict
    spatially-referenced constructs such as food insecurity or
    socio-economic indices. Standard exploratory and confirmatory item
    factor analysis are supported as particular cases, simply by dropping
    the spatial structure.
